What is Polymer Heart Valve Material?
Polymer heart valve materials represent a breakthrough class of synthetic biomaterials engineered to replicate the function of natural heart valves. Unlike traditional mechanical valves (which require lifelong anticoagulation therapy) or bioprosthetic valves (with limited durability), these polymers aim to deliver the ideal balance of flexibility, fatigue resistance, and thromboresistance. Key materials include polyurethanes, polyethylenes, and polypropylene, each offering unique hemodynamic performance characteristics.
These materials are being adopted in next-generation prosthetic valves like Foldax's Tria heart valve (FDA investigational device exemption) and SAT's polymer-based systems - showcasing their potential to disrupt the USD 1.6 billion heart valve industry.
